<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Braccio da Montone</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1368">1368</a>–<a href="/years/1424">1424</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Andrea Fortebraccio</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Braccio da Montone was an Italian condottiere from Perugia, one of the most famous <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenary</a> captains of his age. He seized Perugia in 1416 and ruled it as lord, also extending his power over much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umbria">Umbria</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marche">Marche</a>. He was mortally wounded in 1424 while besieging L'Aquila against the forces of the pope and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/braccio-da-montone.jpg" alt="Braccio da Montone" width="320" height="451" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cristofano dell'Altissimo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Braccio_da_Montone,_portrait_of_Cristofano_dell%27Altissimo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
